{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-47137",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, note that $F\\cup S$ is the event that a randomly selected student in the high school is a girl whose favorite sport is football or a girl whose favorite sport is soccer. \n\nTo estimate the probability of $F\\cup S,$ we\n\n- add up the numbers in the columns **\"Football\"** or **\"Soccer\"** and the row **\"Girls\"**, and\n\n- divide by the total number of data points in the table.\n\nThe numbers in the columns **\"Football\"** or **\"Soccer\"** and the row **\"Girls\"** are highlighted below.\n\n|  | Baseball | Football | Basketball | Soccer | Totals |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Girls | $10$ | $19$ | $10$ | $12$ | $51$ |\n| Boys | $10$ | $13$ | $20$ | $6$ | $49$ |\n| Totals | $20$ | $32$ | $30$ | $18$ | $100$ |\n\nAdding up these numbers and then dividing by the total number of data points in the table $(100),$ we get\n\n$$\nP(F\\cup S)=\\frac{19+12}{100}=\\frac{31}{100}=0.31.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-47137\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>First, note that <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"97\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D439 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c222A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D446 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>S</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> is the event that a randomly selected student in the high school is a girl whose favorite sport is football or a girl whose favorite sport is soccer. </p>\n<p>To estimate the probability of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"98\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D439 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c222A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D446 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> we</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>add up the numbers in the columns <strong>\"Football\"</strong> or <strong>\"Soccer\"</strong> and the row <strong>\"Girls\"</strong>, and</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>divide by the total number of data points in the table.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The numbers in the columns <strong>\"Football\"</strong> or <strong>\"Soccer\"</strong> and the row <strong>\"Girls\"</strong> are highlighted below.</p>\n<table align=\"center\" style=\"border: 1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\" rules=\"all\" cellpadding=\"5\">\n<tbody><tr>\n <td style=\"border-top: 1px solid white; border-left: 1px solid white\"></td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Baseball</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Football</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Basketball</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Soccer</td>\n <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Totals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n  <td bgcolor=\"#F2F4F4\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">Girls</td>\n  <td align=\"center\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"99\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></td>\n  <td align=\"center\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"100\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mstyle style=\"color: blue;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c39\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-mstyle></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mstyle mathcolor=\"blue\"><mn>19</mn></mstyle></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></td>\n  <td align=\"center\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"101\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: rela